        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: review incomplete because event evidence is unavailable\n\nI verified the relevant work order and the September Pending Close time, but **cannot determine whether a cost event was created afterward** from the records I am authorized to read.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–Dekoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not available in accessible evidence |\n| Event amount | Not available in accessible evidence |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available in accessible evidence |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available in accessible evidence |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot conclude without the event’s type, timing, and recorded status |\n\nThe source timestamp contains **no timezone designation**, so I have not inferred one.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied *Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B* documentation, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that new transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are **not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error.\n\n**Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing after Pending Close. Consequently, timing alone is insufficient to judge accounting-status consistency.\n\n### Evidence limitation and disposition\n\nThe accessible task records contain work orders, cost periods, and the policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. Supporting records are restricted to a records-custodian role. I requested an authorized release through the peer and supervisor channels but received none. This absence of accessible evidence **does not establish that no late event exists**.\n\nThe audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_46afe6e0abdc/audit-report.json` and submitted with status **`needs_evidence`**. Completing the review requires an authorized release of the relevant event/source-transaction details. **No database records were changed.**",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
